Input: {"question": "Where is Interstate 235 located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "start": 0, "end": 186, "text": "Interstate 235 (Iowa) Interstate 235 (I-235) in Iowa is an auxiliary Interstate Highway that runs just north of downtown Des Moines through the heart of the Des Moines metropolitan area."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "start": 187, "end": 326, "text": "I-235 runs from the junction of Interstate 35 and Interstate 80 in West Des Moines to the separation of the same two interstates in Ankeny."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "start": 327, "end": 361, "text": "The highway is approximately long."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "start": 362, "end": 519, "text": "I-235, which had seen little improvement since its construction in the 1960s, was completely rebuilt and widened in a project that spanned most of the 2000s."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "start": 520, "end": 599, "text": "Prior to the reconstruction, I-235 had two lanes in each direction with a third"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d01", "start": 0, "end": 137, "text": "sections of I-35 were the 25 miles ( 40 km ) from Ankeny to US 30 near Ames and the 30 miles ( 48 km ) from Ames to US 20 near Williams ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d01", "start": 138, "end": 216, "text": "[ 2 ] By 1972 , I-35 was completed at the Missouri and Minnesota state lines ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d01", "start": 217, "end": 341, "text": "In southern Iowa , the last section , from Iowa 2 near Decatur City to the state line , was completed on December 2 , 1970 ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d01", "start": 342, "end": 449, "text": "In northern Iowa , the section from Iowa 9 near Hanlontown to the state line opened on December 12 , 1972 ."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 0, "end": 138, "text": "one large building housing as many as 28 more toilets than the older buildings , in addition to all the other common rest area amenities ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 139, "end": 188, "text": "They also feature artwork by local Iowa artists ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 189, "end": 242, "text": "[ 7 ] Each new rest area is designed around a theme ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 243, "end": 354, "text": "[ 8 ] [ 9 ] For instance , the facility near Story City celebrates the history of transportation in the state ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 355, "end": 464, "text": "Story County is the home of Iowa DOT and the location where the historic Lincoln Highway and I-35 intersect ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d02", "start": 465, "end": 504, "text": "[ 10 ] Transit [ edit ] Jefferson Lines"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 0, "end": 83, "text": "Drivers continuing south remain within West Des Moines to the Madison County line ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 84, "end": 152, "text": "Suburban areas spread south along the freeway to the Raccoon River ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 153, "end": 254, "text": "02/21/20 West End Throwback West at The loop ramp for Interstate 35 south was previously unnumbered ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 255, "end": 317, "text": "A slight change was also made for the I-235 end sign by 2005 ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 318, "end": 352, "text": "Photo by Dale Sanderson ( 2002 ) ."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d03", "start": 353, "end": 545, "text": "East at Interstate 80 curves east through a six-ramp parclo interchange ( Exit 121 ) with Jordan Creek Parkway on the one mile approach to the West Mixmaster Interchange ( Exit 123 ) with I-35"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d04", "start": 0, "end": 557, "text": "9 East 14th Street East 15th Street Blank Park Zoo , Cownie Sports Complex WESTBOUND : State Capitol Complex 10A EAST East University Avenue EASTBOUND State Fairgrounds East University Avenue State Fairgrounds Sleepy Hollow Sports Park Pleasant Hill 10B TO Easton Boulevard East University Avenue ( 10.8 ) SPEED LIMIT 60 SPEED LIMIT 55 11 Guthrie Avenue 12 East Euclid Avenue Grand View University ( 12.8 ) SPEED LIMIT 65 SPEED LIMIT 60 137A ( 14 ) EAST Davenport 137B ( 14 ) SOUTH WEST Kansas City Council Bluffs END WEST SPEED LIMIT 65 6 lanes ( 3 in each"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0031-17b8770ee026:d00:c0", "entity": "Interstate 235", "scope": "Location", "claim": "Interstate 235 (I-235) in Iowa is an auxiliary Interstate Highway that runs just north of downtown Des Moines through the heart of the Des Moines metropolitan area.", "answer": "Iowa", "quote": "Interstate 235 (Iowa) Interstate 235 (I-235) in Iowa is an auxiliary Interstate Highway that runs just north of downtown Des Moines through the heart of the Des Moines metropolitan area.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["Iowa", "Des Moines metropolitan area"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Iowa", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Des Moines metropolitan area", "origi